    "event_path": "the bayonet's locking and unlocking torque must be reacted by the flange: today only through its seats (the sleeve's end face and the faced bark), because the Zone-3 shank is a Ø9 placeholder in the Ø11 bore — clearance, so it passes none (01_01 §1, HW.8) — unless the flange is held by a tool while the radome turns; the collar is not modelled, so the torque's size is not computed — a lever exists (a tool hold), not a number",
    "text": "A wind torque path onto the anchor's own axis EXISTS: stem torsion turns wood at the bark more than at the tip (ω_r = −½·r·φ′), bending does not. The shank↔sleeve press-fit passes it until the stem-surface torsional shear stress reaches τ_s* = 0.07–2.34 MPa at 20 °C (≤ 1.76 MPa at 40 °C), and at the band floor at 40 °C it carries NOTHING — the shank turns in the sleeve at any torsion. While it holds, the PEEK's shear at the bore is capped by the friction itself at μ·P_c ≤ 0.86 MPa, so the torsional creep §4.3 C was written against cannot build beyond that cap; above it the interface slips by ½·φ′·Δx — a fretting question, not a creep one. «Drop C on the absence of a path» is therefore not available: the path exists."
